# Obsidian SDLC Workflow (v3.1)

**Vault:** `Obisidian-vault-knowledge-base` · Boot: `Prompts/vault-boot.md` · Canon: `System_Rules/00_Agent_Rules_and_Workflow.md`

## Phase sequence (strict)

```
01 Planning → 02 Architecture → 03 DB → 04 API (contracts only)
→ 05 Backend (fix loop → freeze) → 06 Frontend → 07 Integration
→ 08 Perf/Security → 09 Docs → 10 Deploy
```

| Phase | Code? | Rule |
|-------|-------|------|
| 01–04 | No | Vault specs only — no `local_code` implement |
| 05 | Yes | First implement + Policy B tests + **fix loop until green** |
| 06–10 | Yes (UI/ops) | Same repo — **backend frozen** after Phase 05 gate |

## Phase 05 fix loop (explicit)

Backend is **not** frozen during this loop. Repeat until **100% green**:

```
IMPLEMENT → VERIFY (seed · vitest · Playwright API-only)
     ↑              │
     │           FAIL
     └── FIX ←─────┘   (Bug_Log TOP · 1 line per bug)
ALL GREEN → tick checklist → human gate Yes → backend_frozen: true → Phase 06
```

- **Ban:** VERIFIED or gate Yes while any test red or CI deferred/n/a
- **Thrash:** `turns > 8` without gate → HALT → human **Yes** resets `turns: 0` (`stop_reason: fix-loop-continue`)
- **Vault diagram:** `Templates/Phase_05_Fix_Loop.md`

## Backend freeze (after Phase 05 gate Yes)

- Session_State: `backend_frozen: true`
- Phases 06–10: any API/DB/service/migration change → **HALT** → ask human **Yes / No / Modify**
- Post-freeze bug: Scenario C2 — fix only after human Yes, re-run Policy B, re-freeze

## Agent discipline

- Read Session_State first (≤15 lines): `local_code`, `backend_frozen`, `turns`
- DoR required before Phase 05 coding (`stop_reason: dor`)
- Cursor ticks `## Done checklist`; human gates phases only
- ≤2 ECC skills/task · Policy B: vitest + API Playwright (05) · Manual QA UI (06)
- Phase 06+: Hallmark ON for frontend — see `hallmark.mdc`
- Dry-run files: `01_PRD`…`10_Deployment` — never bare `PRD.md` (alias clash)
- Use Obsidian MCP for vault reads/writes when working the SDLC workflow
